\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Measured trends.} Panels (a) and (c) are measurements from the transparent synthetic model ($M{=}738$, $\epsilon {=}\alpha {=}0.05$, provenance-stamped); panels (b) and (d) are measurements from the real-backbone pilot (100 episodes per (config, scenario), 12 configs $=$ \{star, chain, tree, mesh\} $\times $ $N\in \{3,5,10\}$, six open instruct backbones; PILOT-labelled). (a) The per-agent guardrail's $\mathrm  {NRP}_{\mathrm  {sys}}$ advantage over no-defense shrinks across the single-agent, +collusion, +compromised-orchestrator sweep (RQ3); $\mathrm  {NRP}_{\mathrm  {sys}}$ is the ASB-compatible single-agent predicate (\Cref  {tab:degradation}). (b) The compromise-propagation rate orders as chain $<$ tree $<$ star $<$ mesh (\Cref  {prop:chain,prop:star,prop:tree,prop:mesh}, RQ4) and is identical across all six backbones---it is a deterministic structural functional of the topology, so measuring it on one backbone suffices; mesh is now measured and included. (c) Collusion advantage in the unsafe-action channel is clearest at low $\beta $ and converges as $\beta $ grows; under the full system predicate it is masked by availability sabotage on the star hub. (d) Real token cost grows $\approx $ linearly in $N$ for the star topology ($\approx $\,133 tokens/agent); the $\Theta (N^2)$-like mesh growth and $N\in \{20,50\}$ are deferred. No claim of measured superiority beyond these stated configurations is made.}}{27}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{6}{27}{\textbf {Measured trends.} Panels (a) and (c) are measurements from the transparent synthetic model ($M{=}738$, $\epsilon {=}\alpha {=}0.05$, provenance-stamped); panels (b) and (d) are measurements from the real-backbone pilot (100 episodes per (config, scenario), 12 configs $=$ \{star, chain, tree, mesh\} $\times $ $N\in \{3,5,10\}$, six open instruct backbones; PILOT-labelled). (a) The per-agent guardrail's $\NRPs $ advantage over no-defense shrinks across the single-agent, +collusion, +compromised-orchestrator sweep (RQ3); $\NRPs $ is the ASB-compatible single-agent predicate (\Cref {tab:degradation}). (b) The compromise-propagation rate orders as chain $<$ tree $<$ star $<$ mesh (\Cref {prop:chain,prop:star,prop:tree,prop:mesh}, RQ4) and is identical across all six backbones---it is a deterministic structural functional of the topology, so measuring it on one backbone suffices; mesh is now measured and included. (c) Collusion advantage in the unsafe-action channel is clearest at low $\betafrac $ and converges as $\betafrac $ grows; under the full system predicate it is masked by availability sabotage on the star hub. (d) Real token cost grows $\approx $ linearly in $N$ for the star topology ($\approx $\,133 tokens/agent); the $\Theta (N^2)$-like mesh growth and $N\in \{20,50\}$ are deferred. No claim of measured superiority beyond these stated configurations is made}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig:results@cref}{{[figure][6][]6}{[1][25][]27}{}{}{}}
