\newlabel{tab:llm_pilot_topology}{{10}{36}{LLM backbone pilot, topology study (RQ4), \textbf {PILOT-labelled} (Qwen2.5-$\{$0.5$B,$1.5$B,$3$B,$7$B\}$ and Llama-3.2-$\{$1$B,$3$B\}$, $12$ configs $\{$star, chain, tree, mesh$\}$ $\times $ $N\in \{3,5,10\}$, $M{=}100$ per (config, scenario), no defense, fictitious data; numbers excluded from the headlined synthetic tables). $\CPR $ is a deterministic structural functional of the topology and is \emph {identical across all six backbones}, so a single column reports it; it orders exactly as \Cref {prop:chain,prop:star,prop:tree,prop:mesh} predict ($\CPR $: chain $0.130<$ tree $0.198<$ star $0.286<$ mesh $0.627$). $\ASRs $ under the refusing backbones (five of six) is topology-dependent, while Llama-$1$B, which complies, saturates at $\ASRs {=}1.000$ everywhere}{table.caption.38}{}}
